>h2 Overview
>tree open Overview
Cupid OS mounts `.iso` files (ECMA-119 with Rock Ridge names) as read-only
filesystems at arbitrary mount points.
>endtree

>h2 Quick Start
>tree open Quick Start
1. Host-side: build a test ISO:
   `make sync-iso` builds `test_iso/hello.iso` directly from
   the members in `test_iso/fixtures.manifest` with `tools/hostbuild.py`,
   then writes it to the FAT16 disk image as `/hello.iso`. No external ISO
   author is needed.
   Cupid OS exposes that file as `/disk/hello.iso`.

2. Boot CupidOS (`make run`).

3. In shell:

mount /disk/hello.iso /iso

4. `ls /iso` shows `big.bin`, `gen_big.sh`, `jpeg_baseline_8x8.jpg`,
   `long_named_file.txt`, `readme.txt`, and `sub/`.

5. `cat /iso/readme.txt` prints the content.

6. `umount /iso` when done.

[Mount test ISO](shell:mount /disk/hello.iso /iso)
[List mounted ISO](shell:ls /iso)
[Read fixture file](shell:cat /iso/README.TXT)
>endtree

>h2 Features
>tree open Features
  ECMA-119 base format (8.3 uppercase filenames, `;1` versions).
  Rock Ridge NM records provide long names. SUSP CE continuation chains
    are followed up to 8 levels. PX and TF metadata is ignored.
  The repository image keeps its continuation after the directory stream,
    so sequential host readers and Cupid OS see the same Rock Ridge names.
  Case-insensitive path lookups: `/iso/README.TXT` matches `readme.txt`.
    Display names are preserved case.
  Multi-mount: up to 4 ISOs mounted concurrently.
  File I/O: read, seek (SEEK_SET/CUR/END), stat.
  readdir via the standard VFS interface.
>endtree

>h2 Limitations
>tree open Limitations
  Read-only. Write/create/unlink return `-VFS_EACCES`.
  No ATAPI driver. Source must be a `.iso` file accessible via VFS
    (e.g. on FAT16 at `/disk/...` or in homefs at `/home/...`).
  No Joliet. Windows-made Unicode-only ISOs use base names (8.3).
  No symlink traversal. Rock Ridge `SL` records are ignored.
  No deep-tree relocation through CL, PL, or RE records.
  The repository fixture writer rejects more than 8 directory levels.
  4 GB filesize limit (ECMA-119 32-bit LBA).
>endtree

>h2 Architecture
>tree open Architecture
Stack layers (top to bottom):

  shell `mount`
    vfs_mount
      iso9660_vfs  (adapter, 4-slot pool)
        iso9660.cc  (PVD / dir records / SUSP)
          loopdev.cc  (file-backed block_device_t)
            blockcache  (existing LRU sector cache)
              vfs_read on the .iso file

Source files:
  kernel/fs/iso9660.h + iso9660.cc PVD parser, directory walker, SUSP/RR
  kernel/fs/loopdev.cc           file-backed block device adapter
  kernel/fs/iso9660_vfs.cc       VFS mount/open/read/readdir adapter
  tools/hostbuild.py             deterministic test-fixture author
>endtree

>h2 Testing
>tree open Testing
  `test_iso/fixtures/`      checked-in source tree.
  `test_iso/fixtures.manifest` exact build membership.
  `test_iso/hello.iso`      byte-reproducible tracked image.
  `make sync-iso`           rebuilds hello.iso and syncs into the FAT partition.
  `bin/feature17_iso.cc`    checks all 6 root names, reads, and mount reuse.

Run `feature17_iso` from the shell; expect `PASS feature17_iso`.

[Run ISO feature test](shell:cc /bin/feature17_iso.cc)
>endtree

>h2 Verification
>box
How to verify P2 ISO9660:

mount /disk/hello.iso /iso
cat /iso/README.TXT

Expected: file contents printed without error.

[Mount ISO](shell:mount /disk/hello.iso /iso)
[Cat README.TXT](shell:cat /iso/README.TXT)
>endbox

